// @hash cfc66bbe4a72
// @legend — how to write this file (rewritten by ./singularity build; edits inside this block are lost):
//   Item: "<key>" (terse; <key> is "<pluginId>:<id>")
//   Hide: { "item": "<key>", "hidden": true }
//   Spacer (gap): { "type": "spacer", "id": "<unique-id>" } — grows to push every item after it to the far end of the row (title left, chips right); at most one per slot. Use it instead of a second slot.
//   Group: { "type": "header", "label": "<title>", "collapsed": false, "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
//   Overflow (⋯ menu): { "type": "overflow", "id": "<unique-id>", "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
// The server pane, read top to bottom: is it reachable, what is it, how do we
// get in, what does it run.
//
//   status      — liveness first; it is where the old header badge sat, and it
//                 qualifies everything below it.
//   identity    — the record itself (name / host / user / port), plus Delete.
//   ssh-setup   — the key flow. MUST precede deployments: converge and ship
//                 refuse until a probe succeeds, so a reader who meets
//                 Deployments first is offered two verbs that cannot work yet.
//   deployments — what this server actually serves.
//
// Registration order (topo-sort) puts deployments ahead of ssh-setup, which is
// why this file is not just the seeded default.
{
  // Hide: { "item": "<key>", "hidden": true }
  // Spacer (gap): { "type": "spacer", "id": "<unique-id>" }
  // Group: { "type": "header", "label": "<title>", "collapsed": false, "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
  "items": [
    "apps.deploy.health:status",
    "apps.deploy.servers:identity",
    "apps.deploy.ssh-setup:ssh-setup",
    "apps.deploy.deployments:deployments"
  ]
}
